## 3. Solidity (SafeMath - Legacy / Built-in Math)## The Function
Solidity is the language used to write Ethereum Smart Contracts. It uses math routines to execute automated loans, crypto trades, and insurance payouts without human intervention. [13, 14] 
## How It Causes Financial Loss: Integer Overflow / Underflow
Smart contracts process massive numbers representing crypto tokens, but variables have a strict storage limit (e.g., uint8 can only hold numbers from 0 to 255). [15, 16, 17] 

* The Flaw: If a math operation exceeds the maximum limit, it resets back to zero (Overflow). If it goes below zero, it rolls over to the maximum possible number (Underflow). [18, 19, 20, 21, 22] 
* The Exploit: An attacker initiates a crypto token transfer of 1 token when their account balance is 0. If the library fails to validate the subtraction ($0 - 1$), the balance rolls backward to the absolute maximum allowable number ($2^{256}-1$). [23] 
* The Financial Impact: The hacker's account instantly fabricates billions of dollars worth of crypto tokens out of thin air. They can immediately withdraw these tokens, draining the entire liquidity pool of the platform in seconds. [24, 25] 

