## 4. C++ (Boost.Multiprecision)## The Function
Used by banking infrastructure, stock exchanges, and high-performance financial systems for ultra-fast, high-precision mathematical formulas. [26] 
## How It Causes Financial Loss: Buffer Overflow via Malformed Input [27] 
Because C++ values execution speed above all else, mathematical libraries must manually handle computer memory allocation. [28, 29] 

* The Flaw: The library reserves a fixed slot in the computer's RAM to process a numerical input.
* The Exploit: An attacker submits an incredibly massive number or a non-numerical string into a financial input field. The library fails to boundary-check the size, causing the data to overflow the RAM slot.
* The Financial Impact: The overflowing data overwrites the adjacent server code executing in real-time. The hacker alters the active memory to skip the "Check If User Has Sufficient Funds" step, allowing them to transfer millions of dollars out of accounts they do not own.

